= Practice 3 -- Subject-Verb Agreement

== Part A: Choose the correct verb

#table(
  columns: (1fr, 3fr),
  table.header[*\#*][*Answer*],
  [1], [One of my classmates *is* from my country, El Salvador.],
  [2], [Some of the teachers *speak* my language.],
  [3], [Each of the gifts *was* carefully wrapped in gold paper.],
  [4], [One of the words on the test *was* misspelled.],
  [5], [A lot of my classes *were* canceled last week.],
  [6], [A lot of my time *is* spent in the library.],
  [7], [In my country most of the people *want to go* to college.],
  [8], [*Does* anyone know the correct time?],
  [9], [There *are* several kinds of flowers in the bouquet.],
  [10], [There *wasn't* any electricity in our building last night.],
  [11], [The noise from the firecrackers *was* loud.],
)

== Part B: Editing Practice

Correct the six errors in subject-verb agreement in the paragraph *Young Golf Stars*.

#table(
  columns: (1fr, 3fr, 3fr),
  table.header[*Line*][*Error*][*Correction*],
  [2], [Young people around the world *is* taking up the game], [Young people around the world *are* taking up the game],
  [2], [some of them *is* taking it over], [some of them *are* taking it over],
  [3], [One of the young stars *are* Sergio Garcia], [One of the young stars *is* Sergio Garcia],
  [8], [both *has* ethnic backgrounds], [both *have* ethnic backgrounds],
  [11], [Each of these two young Americans *have* shocked the world], [Each of these two young Americans *has* shocked the world],
  [14], [all three of these young golfers *has* great futures], [all three of these young golfers *have* great futures],
)

*Note:* The subject determines the verb. Watch for prepositional phrases between the subject and verb -- the subject is never inside the prepositional phrase.
